'' AN OPERATOR DECLARED AND DEFINED SEPARATELY is ONE operator. Collect pairs a
'' definition with its declaration by ARITY, and every binary operator has the same
'' arity -- so a set of three '-' declarations left each definition to declare a symbol
'' of its own, the duplicates cost identically, and NO operator bound at all. That is
'' how fb/chrono.bi declares its twelve, and it is the same fix the ordinary call
'' picker already had: two candidates that MANGLE ALIKE are one procedure, and the one
'' with a body wins.
''
'' PARENTHESES ARE TRANSPARENT TO AN ADDRESS. '( ( d + s ) - s ).ticks' wraps the inner
'' operator in a paren; with no case for one, the address fell through to the value
'' path, which stored the RESULT POINTER into a fresh aggregate temporary -- an address
'' where the object belonged.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/operator-split.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/operator-split.out
